From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: do not take a translated MLD MAC address as the link address in handle_auth()

When a non-AP MLD that the driver already knows (e.g., a still
associated station starting FT authentication towards the same AP MLD)
sends an Authentication frame, the driver translates the link address
in the SA field to the MLD MAC address. handle_auth() then stored that
MLD MAC address as the link address of the association link and, in the
FT case, ap_sta_re_add() created the driver STA entry with it, so the
station's frames sent from its real link address were no longer matched
and the association was dead until the station gave up and associated
from scratch.

Keep the previously learned link address when the SA of such an
Authentication frame is the MLD MAC address of a station for which a
different link address is already known.

Signed-off-by: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -4450,23 +4450,50 @@
 	 * peer_addr based on mgmt->sa which would have been translated to the
 	 * MLD MAC address. */
 	if (!sta->added_unassoc && auth_transaction == 1) {
+		u8 prev_peer_addr[ETH_ALEN];
+
+		os_memcpy(prev_peer_addr,
+			  sta->mld_info.links[hapd->mld_link_id].peer_addr,
+			  ETH_ALEN);
 		ap_sta_free_sta_profile(&sta->mld_info);
 		os_memset(&sta->mld_info, 0, sizeof(sta->mld_info));
 
 		if (mld_sta) {
 			u8 link_id = hapd->mld_link_id;
+			const u8 *link_addr = mgmt->sa;
 
 			ap_sta_set_mld(sta, true);
 			sta->mld_assoc_link_id = link_id;
 
 			/*
+			 * The driver translates the link address of a non-AP
+			 * MLD it already knows (e.g., a still associated
+			 * station that starts FT authentication) to the MLD
+			 * MAC address in received frames. Do not take such an
+			 * SA as the link address; keep the link address learned
+			 * from the earlier Authentication or (Re)Association
+			 * Request frame instead, so that the driver STA entry
+			 * is (re)created with the address the station really
+			 * uses on this link.
+			 */
+			if (ether_addr_equal(mgmt->sa, sa) &&
+			    !is_zero_ether_addr(prev_peer_addr) &&
+			    !ether_addr_equal(prev_peer_addr, sa)) {
+				wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
+					   "MLD: Keep link address " MACSTR
+					   " for " MACSTR " (SA is the MLD MAC address)",
+					   MAC2STR(prev_peer_addr), MAC2STR(sa));
+				link_addr = prev_peer_addr;
+			}
+
+			/*
 			 * Set the MLD address as the station address and the
 			 * station addresses.
 			 */
 			os_memcpy(sta->mld_info.common_info.mld_addr, sa,
 				  ETH_ALEN);
 			os_memcpy(sta->mld_info.links[link_id].peer_addr,
-				  mgmt->sa, ETH_ALEN);
+				  link_addr, ETH_ALEN);
 			os_memcpy(sta->mld_info.links[link_id].local_addr,
 				  hapd->own_addr, ETH_ALEN);
 		}
